      "math_academy_id": "q-46088",
      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "An adult says $11\\,400$ words in $60$ minutes. If we want to determine the average of words spoken per minute, we use the formula $P=\\frac{w}{t},$ being $w$ the total number of words and $t$ the time in minutes.\n\nIn words, what is the appropriate measurement unit for $P?$",
      "worked_solution": "We are solving for measurement units, so we can ignore the quantities $11\\,400$ and $60.$ They do not matter, if we are just solving for units.\n\nSince $w$ represents $\\text{words}$ and $t$ represents $\\text{minute},$ the appropriate measurement unit for $P=\\frac{w}{t}$ is $\\frac{\\text{words}}{\\text{minute}},$ that is, 'words per minute'.",
